{"id":"c99b143f-7e06-4b8d-b198-10b875faf4e7","object":"chat.completion","created":1784818119,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    lines = case['payload']['lines']\\n    records = []\\n    valid = True\\n    violation = None\\n    state = 'START'\\n    expected = {\\n        'START': ['Thought'],\\n        'AFTER_THOUGHT': ['Action', 'Final'],\\n        'AFTER_ACTION': ['Action Input', 'Observation'],\\n        'AFTER_ACTION_INPUT': ['Observation'],\\n        'AFTER_OBSERVATION': ['Thought', 'Final']\\n    }\\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines, 1):\\n        if ':' not in line:\\n            valid = False\\n            violation = {'line': i, 'prefix': records[:]}\\n            break\\n        parts = line.split(':', 1)\\n        raw_type = parts[0].strip()\\n        content = parts[1].strip() if len(parts) > 1 else ''\\n        low_type = raw_type.lower()\\n        type_map = {\\n            'thought': 'Thought',\\n            'action': 'Action',\\n            'action input': 'Action Input',\\n            'observation': 'Observation',\\n            'final': 'Final'\\n        }\\n        canonical = type_map.get(low_type)\\n        if canonical is None:\\n            valid = False\\n            violation = {'line': i, 'prefix': records[:]}\\n            break\\n        allowed = expected.get(state, [])\\n        if canonical not in allowed:\\n            valid = False\\n            violation = {'line': i, 'prefix': records[:]}\\n            break\\n        if canonical == 'Final' and i != len(lines):\\n            valid = False\\n            violation = {'line': i, 'prefix': records[:]}\\n            break\\n        record = {'type': low_type, 'content': content}\\n        records.append(record)\\n        if canonical == 'Thought':\\n            state = 'AFTER_THOUGHT'\\n        elif canonical == 'Action':\\n            state = 'AFTER_ACTION'\\n        elif canonical == 'Action Input':\\n            state = 'AFTER_ACTION_INPUT'\\n        elif canonical == 'Observation':\\n            state = 'AFTER_OBSERVATION'\\n        elif canonical == 'Final':\\n            state = 'END'\\n        if not valid:\\n            break\\n    if valid and (not records or records[-1]['type'] != 'final'):\\n        valid = False\\n        line_num = len(lines)\\n        violation = {'line': line_num, 'prefix': records[:-1]}\\n        records = records[:-1]\\n    result = {'valid': valid, 'records': records}\\n    if violation is not None:\\n        result['violation'] = violation\\n    return result\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a Python function `solve(case)` that parses lines from case['payload']['lines']. The task is to parse Thought, Action, Observation, Final records. The expected output: return a JSON-serializable object. Likely we need to validate interleaved pattern: Thought then Action then Observation for nonterminal cycles, Final only at the end. On violation, return line number and valid prefix. Also return lowercase typed trajectory records and validity flag.\n\nFrom the fixture, the cases have lines like: \"Thought: inspect\", \"Action: lookup\", \"Observation: found\", \"Thought: answer\", \"Final: done\". So the pattern: each line starts with a type (Thought, Action, Observation, Final) followed by colon and content. We need to parse these.\n\nThe function should return something like:\n{\n  \"valid\": true/false,\n  \"records\": [{\"type\": \"thought\", \"content\": \"inspect\"}, ...],\n  \"violation\": null or {\"line\": int, \"prefix\": list of records up to before violation}\n}\n\nBut we need to look at the specification: \"Return lowercase typed trajectory records and an explicit validity flag. On the first violation return its one-based line and the valid prefix.\"\n\nSo output should include validity flag, list of records (lowercase types), and if invalid, violation line and prefix (list of records up to before